  "body": "Bulk update (`PUT /api/v2/tasks/bulk`, MCP `tasks_bulk_update`) wrote more than `fields` named: assignees, reminders, `is_favorite` reset from cloned `values` on every task. Missing/empty `fields` did full replace, wiping description, dates, priority etc. Breaks documented \"rest of each task is left untouched\".\r\n\r\nFixes #4109\r\nCloses #4110 (assignees commit cherry-picked, authorship kept).\r\n\r\n- `assignees`, `reminders`, `is_favorite` only written when named in `fields`; accepted as bulk fields.\r\n- Missing/empty `fields` rejected: `ErrBulkTaskFieldsRequired` (code 4036).\r\n\r\n## Behaviour changes\r\n\r\n- The empty-`fields` check lives in `BulkTask.CanUpdate`, so it also applies to v1 `POST /api/v1/tasks/bulk`, which shares the model. v1 requests without `fields` now get a 400 instead of silently overwriting every task.\r\n- Because reminders are now preserved, a bulk update that clears a date which a relative reminder depends on fails with `ErrReminderRelativeToMissing`, the same as a single-task update does.\r\n\r\n## How to verify\r\n\r\nSetup: a task `$TASK` with one assignee, one reminder, and marked as favorite by the calling user.\r\n\r\n1. Run `curl -X PUT \"$URL/api/v2/tasks/bulk\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d \"{\\\"task_ids\\\":[$TASK],\\\"fields\\\":[\\\"priority\\\"],\\\"values\\\":{\\\"priority\\\":3}}\"`.\r\n2. Fetch the task with `GET /api/v2/tasks/$TASK`.\r\n3. **Expected:** priority is 3, and the assignee, the reminder and `is_favorite: true` are all still there.\r\n   **Before this PR:** assignees and reminders were empty and `is_favorite` was false.\r\n\r\n1. Send the same request with `\"fields\":[\"reminders\"]` and `\"values\":{\"reminders\":[{\"reminder\":\"2030-01-01T12:00:00Z\"}]}`.\r\n2. **Expected:** the task has exactly that one reminder; priority, assignees and the favorite state are unchanged.\r\n\r\n1. Send the request from step 1 without the `fields` key, then again with `\"fields\":[]`.\r\n2. **Expected:** both return 400 with `\"code\":4036`, and the task is unchanged.\r\n   **Before this PR:** 200, and the description, dates, priority and color were cleared.",
